<h1>5. How the System Works: End-to-End Workflow</h1>
<div class="diagram-box">
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      MARG END-TO-END SYSTEM PIPELINE                        │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 1. USER INPUT: Start & Goal Coordinates, Preference Weights, Max Deviation  │
│                                    │                                        │
│ 2. GEODESIC PROJECTION: Maps WGS84 (Lat/Lon) to local UTM Metric (X/Y)     │
│    • Zones 42N to 47N auto-selected across Indian longitudes (68°E–97.5°E)  │
│                                    │                                        │
│ 3. SMART ENDPOINT SNAPPING: BFS radial ring search relocates origin/goal    │
│    if dropped inside Sanctuary, Slope > 30°, Water Body, or Heritage Site  │
│                                    │                                        │
│ 4. COMPOSITE COST SURFACE: 13 layers evaluated on 250m metric grid nodes    │
│    • Directional skew penalties added for rivers, railways, faults, power   │
│                                    │                                        │
│ 5. METRIC A* PATHFINDING: Priority queue search with Octile Heuristic       │
│    • Admissible distance: h = dx + dy + (sqrt(2) - 2) * min(dx, dy)         │
│                                    │                                        │
│ 6. LAGRANGIAN RELAXATION: Enforces length budget L <= L_base * (1 + delta)  │
│    • If unconstrained fits budget -> instant return                         │
│    • Otherwise adapts lambda multiplier across 8 binary search iterations   │
│                                    │                                        │
│ 7. 2D RIGHT-OF-WAY (RoW) BUFFER ENGINE (JTS Topology Suite):                │
│    • 60m Direct RoW | 100m Construction Clearance | 250m Environmental Zone │
│    • 5-point transverse cross-sectional audit every 125m along chainage     │
│                                    │                                        │
│ 8. HIGHWAY NETWORK PLANNER: Autonomous post-mainline engineering            │
│    • IRC Interchanges placed (spacing >= 15 km, local slope <= 12°)         │
│    • Secondary A* Feeder Spurs routed to intermediate mandis / tehsils      │
│    • Structural inventory classified: ROBs, Flyovers, Bridges, Eco-Ducts    │
│                                    │                                        │
│ 9. MULTI-CRITERIA EVALUATION & EXPLAINABILITY:                             │
│    • 4-Pillar Scores (0–100) & Composite Alignment Index (CAI)              │
│    • Wildlife (Protection) Act, 1972 statutory clearance compliance report  │
│    • Indicative Bill of Quantities (BoQ) & Capital Expenditure (₹ Crore)    │
│                                    │                                        │
│ 10. OUTPUT: GeoJSON FeatureCollection streamed to React + Leaflet UI        │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
</div>

<h1>6. Mathematical Formulations</h1>

<h3>1. Ellipsoidal Transverse Mercator Projections (WGS84 to UTM)</h3>
<p>To eliminate degree distortion, geographic coordinates (&phi;, &lambda;) on the WGS84 ellipsoid (a = 6,378,137.0 m, f = 1/298.257223563) are transformed into metric Easting (X) and Northing (Y) coordinates via:</p>
<div class="formula-box">
X = k0 &middot; N &middot; [ A + (1 - T + C)(A^3 / 6) + (5 - 18T + T^2 + 72C - 58e'^2)(A^5 / 120) ] + X0<br><br>
Y = k0 &middot; [ M - M0 + N &middot; tan(&phi;) &middot; [ A^2 / 2 + (5 - T + 9C + 4C^2)(A^4 / 24) + (61 - 58T + T^2 + 600C - 330e'^2)(A^6 / 720) ] ]
</div>
<p>Where k0 = 0.9996, X0 = 500,000 m (false easting), &lambda;0 is the central meridian of the UTM zone, A = (&lambda; - &lambda;0)cos(&phi;), N is the radius of curvature in the prime vertical, and M is the meridional distance from the equator.</p>

<h3>2. Admissible Metric Octile Distance Heuristic</h3>
<p>On an 8-connected grid with orthogonal step &Delta;s = 250 m and diagonal step &radic;2 &times; &Delta;s &approx; 353.55 m, MARG applies the Octile metric distance heuristic:</p>
<div class="formula-box">
h(u, goal) = &Delta;x_metric + &Delta;y_metric + (&radic;2 - 2) &middot; min(&Delta;x_metric, &Delta;y_metric)
</div>
<p>Where &Delta;x_metric = |X_u - X_goal| and &Delta;y_metric = |Y_u - Y_goal|. This heuristic is strictly admissible (never overestimates physical movement cost), guaranteeing optimal A* convergence.</p>

<h3>3. Dual-Stage Lagrangian Relaxation for Length Constraints</h3>
<p>To solve the constrained optimization problem: <code>Minimize C(&pi;) subject to L(&pi;) &le; L_max = L_baseline &times; (1 + &delta;_max / 100)</code>:</p>
<div class="formula-box">
L(&pi;, &lambda;) = C(&pi;) + &lambda; &middot; (L(&pi;) - L_max) &implies; C_&lambda;(e) = C(e) + &lambda; &middot; d(e)
</div>
<p>If the unconstrained route exceeds the length budget, the multiplier &lambda; is iteratively increased across successive A* runs to penalize physical detours, steering the corridor back toward the direct baseline until the budget is satisfied.</p>

<h3>4. Skew-Angle Crossing Penalty Formulation</h3>
<p>Civil engineering costs for crossing linear barriers (rivers, railways, active faults, and power lines) increase inversely with the sine of intersection angle &theta;_intersect:</p>
<div class="formula-box">
&Omega;_crossing(u, v) = &Omega;_base &middot; [ 1.0 + &kappa;_skew &middot; |cos(&theta;_intersect)| ]
</div>
<p>An orthogonal crossing (&theta; = 90&deg;) incurs only &Omega;_base, whereas acute crossings (&theta; &rarr; 0&deg;) penalize parallel running along barrier boundaries.</p>

<h3>5. Four-Pillar Scoring & Composite Alignment Index (CAI)</h3>
<p>Corridor quality is scored across four normalized pillars (Score &isin; [0, 100]):</p>
<ul>
    <li><b>Environmental Conservation Score (S_env):</b><br>
    <code>S_env = max(5.0, 100.0 - [0.45&middot;A_forest + 1.20&middot;A_wetland + 0.02&middot;L_bridge + 3.50&middot;N_wildlife + 12.0&middot;L_sanctuary])</code></li>
    <li><b>Social Safeguard Score (S_soc):</b><br>
    <code>S_soc = max(5.0, 100.0 - [1.50&middot;P_displaced + 2.20&middot;N_buildings + 4.00&middot;N_settlements])</code></li>
    <li><b>Directness & Economy Score (S_dir):</b><br>
    <code>S_dir = max(10.0, 100.0 - [2.50&middot;&delta;_percent + 1.20&middot;N_structures])</code></li>
    <li><b>Regional Connectivity Score (S_conn):</b><br>
    <code>S_conn = min(100.0, 30.0 + 15.0&middot;N_spurs + 10.0&middot;log10(P_served + 1) - 0.50&middot;L_spur)</code></li>
</ul>
<div class="formula-box">
Composite Alignment Index (CAI) = [ w_env&middot;S_env + w_soc&middot;S_soc + w_dir&middot;S_dir + 1.0&middot;S_conn ] / [ w_env + w_soc + w_dir + 1.0 ]
</div>

<h1>7. Steps to Build / Reproduce the Model</h1>
<ol>
    <li><b>Environment Setup:</b> Install OpenJDK Java 25 and Apache Maven 3.9+. Install Node.js v20+ LTS and npm for the frontend. Core dependencies: Spring Boot 3.5, LocationTech JTS Core (topology and buffer operations), GeoTools Coverage & GeoTIFF (raster reading), and Jackson (JSON serialization).</li>
    <li><b>Geospatial Data Preparation:</b> Harvest ISRO Bhuvan WMS layers (1:50,000 LULC and flood rasters) with local disk caching. Process CartoDEM/SRTM 30m elevation models to derive slope rasters in metric UTM projection using GDAL Horn's algorithm. Ingest OpenStreetMap vector layers (rivers, roads, railways, power lines, building footprints) and 780+ Indian district census catalogs.</li>
    <li><b>Projection & Metric Grid Setup:</b> Implement analytical ellipsoidal Transverse Mercator transformations covering Indian UTM Zones 42N to 47N. Discretize the bounding corridor search space into an 8-connected grid with uniform 250 m metric spacing.</li>
    <li><b>Cost Layer Construction:</b> Implement the 13 CostLayer interfaces. Each layer assesses node coordinates and edge movements against raster samples and vector indices. Combine all 13 layers into a CompositeCostSurface with request-scoped dynamic weight multipliers.</li>
    <li><b>A* Search with Lagrangian Relaxation:</b> Implement the metric A* priority queue using the admissible Octile heuristic. Wrap the search in a dual-stage Lagrangian Relaxation loop to enforce route length limits. Implement BFS Smart Snapping for prohibited endpoints.</li>
    <li><b>Post-Mainline Network Engineering:</b> Implement HighwayNetworkPlannerService to place interchanges (&ge; 15 km spacing, &le; 12&deg; slope), route secondary A* feeder spurs to regional mandis, and classify structural crossings (ROBs, flyovers, bridges, eco-ducts). Build 2D RoW polygons with 5-point transverse swath auditing.</li>
    <li><b>Evaluation & UI Integration:</b> Implement TradeOffEvaluationService for 4-pillar scoring, BoQ calculation, and statutory compliance auditing. Build the React + Leaflet frontend and sync static assets into Spring Boot's static resources directory for unified single-port deployment on port 8080.</li>
</ol>

